  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "Tune a classifier that identifies a player as \"about to quit\" or \"keeps playing.\" To make this prediction, the classifier uses:\r\n\r\n- How many minutes the player played this week (`time`).\r\n- The furthest level they’ve gotten to in the game (`levels`).\r\n\r\nCurrently, the classifier looks at only one nearest neighbor.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Run the program. What is the accuracy of the classifier when `n_neighbors` is 1?\r\n- Write a loop that tries every setting in the `n_neighbors` list, printing the classifier’s accuracy for each value.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember a `for` loop allows you to iterate over a list of values.\r\n\r\n```\r\nn_neighbors = [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15]\r\nfor n_neighbor in n_neighbors:\r\n  ...\r\n```",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
